iii
ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS 
Many institutions and businesses supported the work of the 2020 National Population and Housing 
Census.  These include the Ministry of Finance and Economic Management, the Department of Local 
Authorities for their fieldwork support, the Vanuatu Christian Council, the National Youth Council, 
the Malvatumauri National Council of Chiefs, and Vanuatu Broadcasting and Television Corporation 
for their support with public awareness and cooperation, Air Vanuatu for their support with training 
and fieldwork logistics, and Digicel Vanuatu.  The VNSO wishes to extend our gratitude to these 
organizations for enabling the successful collection of census data.   
My appreciation is extended to the Pacific Community (SPC) Statistics for Development Division, as 
well as to Mr. Geoffrey Hayes, for the technical assistance provided.  I also acknowledge the indirect 
support of the European Union in acquiring new tablets that were used for the census, as well as 
financial support from the UNFPA supporting technical assistance as well as piloting of the census 
instruments.   
I would also like to thank the former Government Statistician, Mr Kap Andy Calo, and the 2020 
National Population and Housing Census team, led by the Census Coordinator, Mr. Jimmy Tamkela, 
and his assistant, Ms. Grace Tabi.  The advice and guidance given to them by members of the Census 
Steering Committee, including the late Ps. Alan Nafuki, bolstered their success in completing a 
national census in the midst of an uncertain global pandemic.  The encouragement and trust given 
by the Census Steering Committee has enabled us to have this critical data available today.   
Lastly and most importantly, to the Government and people of Vanuatu, I extend my sincerest 
thanks and gratitude for your invaluable cooperation, support, and participation in the 2020 
National Population and Housing Census.   
In gratitude, 
 
 
 
Mr Benuel Lenge 
Government Statistician 
Vanuatu National Statistics Office 
Republic of Vanuatu 
 
Acknowledgements
