Concept Definition
Canoe with motor: Traditional canoes however it is propelled using the help of a
motor engine instead of using a paddle
Median age  the age that divides a population into two numerically equal groups - that is, half
the people are younger than this age and half are older. It is a single index that
summarizes the age distribution of a population.
Own Account work done on their own without hiring other non-member of the household,
include the type of job defined as "a self-employment job" and have not engaged
on a continuous basis any "employees" to work for them during the reference
period
Person  any individual member of the household or institution who is present on the census
night and is therefore counted in the census. This includes everyone: young and old,
male of female, expatriates or residents, tourist and locals alike. For census
purposes, the term “person” denotes each individual falling within the scope of
census. A person can be identified as belonging to the household population or to
the institutional population where he or she slept on the night
Usual place of residence is defined for census purposes as the place a person last lived for six months or more
or intends to live for at least six months.
